---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import CopyCommand from '../components/copyCommand';
import { installCommand, releasesUrl } from '../lib/nav';
import { withBase } from '../lib/base';

// Every terminal transcript on this page was captured from lattice 1.1.1
// running against a two-package npm repo. Re-capture them rather than editing by hand.
const initOutput = `✓ wrote lattice.json
✓ wrote .lattice/schema.json
✓ updated .gitignore

2 workspaces:
  app    npm      build test
  greet  npm      build

next: lattice run build`;

const config = `{
  "$schema": ".lattice/schema.json",
  "latticeVersion": "1.1.1"
}`;

const dryRun = `❖ lattice  dry run · build
  → greet:build  npm run build
  → app:build  npm run build`;

const coldRun = `❖ lattice  build  · 2 workspaces

  ✓ greet  0.12s
  ✓ app    0.12s

❖  2 tasks  0.27s`;

const warmRun = `❖ lattice  build  · 2 workspaces

  ● greet  cached · 0.12s saved
  ● app    cached · 0.12s saved

❖  2 tasks · 2 cached  0.00s · 0.23s saved

❖❖❖ FULL POWER`;

const windowsInstallCommand = 'irm https://latticeandcompany.github.io/lattice/install.ps1 | iex';

const next = [
	{
		name: 'Installation',
		href: withBase('/docs/installation'),
		blurb: 'Supported platforms, building from source, shell completions, and how to remove it.',
	},
	{
		name: 'Workspaces',
		href: withBase('/docs/workspaces'),
		blurb: 'Where Lattice finds your workspaces, what it names them, and how it orders them.',
	},
	{
		name: 'Caching',
		href: withBase('/docs/caching'),
		blurb: 'What goes into a task hash, and what makes a cached result valid to restore.',
	},
	{
		name: 'Toolchains',
		href: withBase('/docs/toolchains'),
		blurb: 'Pin the version of node, rust, go, or any other tool your repo builds against.',
	},
];
---

<Layout
	title="Get started · Lattice"
	description="Install Lattice in a repo, let it find your workspaces, and run a build that comes back from cache the second time."
>
	<section class="px-3 pt-5 pb-4">
		<div class="mx-auto" style="max-width: 48rem;">
			<h1 class="fw-bold mb-3" style="font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 3.75rem); letter-spacing: -0.03em;">
				Get started
			</h1>
			<p class="fs-5 mb-0" style="color: var(--text-muted);">
				Six steps from a repo with no Lattice in it to a build that comes back from cache the second time
				you run it. You need a terminal and the tools your workspaces already use. The transcripts are
				from a repo with two npm packages, <code>app</code> and <code>greet</code>, where
				<code>app</code> depends on <code>greet</code>.
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="px-3 pb-5">
		<ol class="steps mx-auto list-unstyled mb-0" style="max-width: 48rem;">
			<li class="step">
				<span class="step__num" aria-hidden="true">1</span>
				<div class="step__body">
					<h2 class="step__title">Install it into your repo</h2>
					<p>From the root of the repo you want to use Lattice in:</p>
					<CopyCommand client:visible command={installCommand} />
					<p class="mt-3">
						The script picks the archive for your platform, checks its SHA-256 against the release's
						published checksums, and refuses to install on a mismatch. The binary lands in
						<code>.lattice/bin/</code>, and the script adds that path to your <code>.gitignore</code> if
						the repo already has one. The only thing it writes outside the repo is a <code>PATH</code>
						line in your shell config. To skip that line, pass <code>--no-modify-path</code> and call
						<code>./.lattice/bin/lattice</code> directly.
					</p>
					<p>
						That script covers macOS, Linux, and Windows under Git Bash. In PowerShell, run the
						Windows installer instead:
					</p>
					<pre class="step__code"><code>{windowsInstallCommand}</code></pre>
					<p class="mb-0">
						It writes the same <code>.lattice\bin</code> and adds that directory to your user
						<code>PATH</code>, asking first. Every published build is listed on the
						<a href={releasesUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">releases page</a>. See
						<a href={withBase('/docs/installation')}>Installation</a> for the switches both
						installers take.
					</p>
				</div>
			</li>

			<li class="step">
				<span class="step__num" aria-hidden="true">2</span>
				<div class="step__body">
					<h2 class="step__title">Check that it runs</h2>
					<pre class="step__code"><code>lattice --version</code></pre>
					<pre class="step__code step__code--out"><code>lattice 1.1.1</code></pre>
					<p class="mb-0">
						If your shell can't find <code>lattice</code>, open a new terminal so the
						<code>PATH</code> line takes effect.
					</p>
				</div>
			</li>

			<li class="step">
				<span class="step__num" aria-hidden="true">3</span>
				<div class="step__body">
					<h2 class="step__title">Initialize</h2>
					<pre class="step__code"><code>lattice init</code></pre>
					<p>
						<code>init</code> reads the repo before it writes anything. It finds the workspaces your
						<code>package.json</code>, <code>pnpm-workspace.yaml</code>, <code>Cargo.toml</code> or
						<code>go.work</code> already name, and on a terminal it offers any other projects it found
						and any tool versions the repo already pins. <code>-y</code> takes what it offers without
						asking. Then it shows every workspace it sees, the tool that runs it and the tasks it can
						run:
					</p>
					<pre class="step__code step__code--out"><code>{initOutput}</code></pre>
					<p class="mb-0">
						Commit <code>lattice.json</code> and <code>.lattice/schema.json</code>, which lets your
						editor check the config as you type. <code>init</code> gitignores the rest of
						<code>.lattice/</code>, which is per-machine.
					</p>
				</div>
			</li>
			<li class="step">
				<span class="step__num" aria-hidden="true">4</span>
				<div class="step__body">
					<h2 class="step__title">Read what it wrote</h2>
					<pre class="step__code step__code--file"><code>{config}</code></pre>
					<p>
						That is the whole config for this repo. The packages come from the root
						<code>package.json</code>'s <code>workspaces</code>, the tool from the lockfile, the tasks
						from each package's <code>scripts</code>, and the order from <code>app</code>'s dependency on
						<code>greet</code>. Ask what a run would do before running it:
					</p>
					<pre class="step__code"><code>lattice run build --dry-run</code></pre>
					<pre class="step__code step__code--out"><code>{dryRun}</code></pre>
					<p class="mb-0">
						A project no workspace file names, a dependency between languages, or a command you want to
						write yourself goes in <code>lattice.json</code>. See
						<a href={withBase('/docs/configuration')}>Configuration</a>.
					</p>
				</div>
			</li>
			<li class="step">
				<span class="step__num" aria-hidden="true">5</span>
				<div class="step__body">
					<h2 class="step__title">Install dependencies</h2>
					<pre class="step__code"><code>lattice setup</code></pre>
					<p class="mb-0">
						<code>setup</code> checks or installs any tool versions you pinned, then runs each
						workspace's own installer, once per lockfile: here, one <code>npm install</code>. Run it as
						often as you like. Lattice skips a workspace whose lockfile hasn't changed.
					</p>
				</div>
			</li>

			<li class="step">
				<span class="step__num" aria-hidden="true">6</span>
				<div class="step__body">
					<h2 class="step__title">Run a task</h2>
					<pre class="step__code"><code>lattice run build</code></pre>
					<pre class="step__code step__code--out"><code>{coldRun}</code></pre>
					<p>
						<code>greet</code> builds before <code>app</code> because <code>app</code> depends on it.
						Workspaces with no dependency between them run at the same time. While a run is going, the
						live display shows each running task with the last lines it printed and what the rest are
						waiting on; in CI, or with <code>--stream</code>, you get one plain line per event instead.
					</p>
					<p>Run it again without changing a file:</p>
					<pre class="step__code step__code--out"><code>{warmRun}</code></pre>
					<p class="mb-0">
						Nothing changed, so nothing ran. Each package's <code>dist/</code> came back out of
						<code>.lattice/cache/</code>. Edit a file in <code>greet</code> and it builds again, and so
						does <code>app</code>, which depends on it. Run it from inside <code>packages/greet</code>
						and only <code>greet</code> builds.
					</p>
				</div>
			</li>
		</ol>
	</section>

	<section class="px-3 pb-5">
		<div class="mx-auto" style="max-width: 48rem;">
			<h2 class="fw-bold mb-4" style="font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 3.5vw, 2.25rem); letter-spacing: -0.02em;">
				Where to go next
			</h2>
			<div class="row g-3">
				{
					next.map((item) => (
						<div class="col-12 col-sm-6">
							<a href={item.href} class="card h-100 text-decoration-none next-card">
								<div class="card-body p-4">
									<span class="d-flex align-items-center gap-2 fw-bold mb-2" style="color: var(--text);">
										{item.name}
										<i class="bi bi-arrow-right next-card__arrow" aria-hidden="true" />
									</span>
									<span class="d-block mb-0" style="color: var(--text-subtle); line-height: 1.6;">
										{item.blurb}
									</span>
								</div>
							</a>
						</div>
					))
				}
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>
</Layout>

<style>
	.steps {
		counter-reset: step;
	}
	.step {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: 2.5rem 1fr;
		column-gap: 1.25rem;
		padding-bottom: 3rem;
	}
	.step:last-child {
		padding-bottom: 0;
	}
	/* The rail runs through the number and down to the next step, so the sequence
	   reads as one thread rather than six detached blocks. */
	.step__num {
		position: relative;
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
		justify-content: center;
		width: 2.5rem;
		height: 2.5rem;
		border: 1px solid var(--border);
		border-radius: 6px;
		background: var(--surface);
		font-family: 'DM Mono', monospace;
		font-size: 0.95rem;
		color: var(--focus);
	}
	.step:not(:last-child) .step__num::after {
		content: '';
		position: absolute;
		top: 2.5rem;
		bottom: -3rem;
		left: 50%;
		width: 1px;
		background: var(--border-subtle);
	}
	.step__title {
		margin: 0.25rem 0 0.75rem;
		font-size: 1.5rem;
		font-weight: 700;
		letter-spacing: -0.01em;
	}
	.step__body :global(p) {
		color: var(--text-subtle);
		line-height: 1.65;
	}
	.step__body :global(code) {
		font-family: 'DM Mono', monospace;
		font-size: 0.85em;
		color: var(--text);
	}
	.step__code {
		margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
		padding: 0.85rem 1rem;
		border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
		border-radius: 6px;
		background: var(--surface-2);
		font-family: 'DM Mono', monospace;
		font-size: 0.82rem;
		line-height: 1.7;
		overflow-x: auto;
	}
	.step__code::before {
		content: '$ ';
		color: var(--text-muted);
	}
	.step__code--out::before,
	.step__code--file::before {
		content: none;
	}
	.step__code--out {
		color: var(--text-muted);
	}
	@media (max-width: 575.98px) {
		.step {
			grid-template-columns: 2rem 1fr;
			column-gap: 0.9rem;
		}
		.step__num {
			width: 2rem;
			height: 2rem;
			font-size: 0.85rem;
		}
		.step:not(:last-child) .step__num::after {
			top: 2rem;
		}
	}
</style>
